---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PlaceholderBanner from '../components/PlaceholderBanner.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema, organizationSchema } from '../utils/schema';

const description =
  'Josh rents a flat, grows food on a small balcony, and writes down what works. The story behind Pot and Balcony and where it is heading.';

const personSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About Josh and Pot and Balcony',
  url: `${SITE.url}/about/`,
  mainEntity: { '@type': 'Person', name: SITE.author.name, jobTitle: SITE.author.role, url: `${SITE.url}/about/` },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Josh and Pot and Balcony"
  description={description}
  jsonLd={[personSchema, breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]), organizationSchema()]}
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container about-hero">
      <div>
        <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'About' }]} />
        <p class="kicker">About</p>
        <h1>Hi, I&rsquo;m Josh.</h1>
        <p class="lede">I rent a flat, I have a small balcony, and I&rsquo;m learning to grow food on it &mdash; properly, in public.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="about-photo">
        <!-- PLACEHOLDER: replace with a real photo of Josh -->
        <img src={SITE.author.avatar} alt="Placeholder portrait of Josh" width="400" height="400" fetchpriority="high" />
        <figcaption>that&rsquo;s me <em>(real photo soon)</em></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="page-body">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <PlaceholderBanner>
        This About page is a draft skeleton. Everything in [square brackets] needs Josh&rsquo;s real details and voice. Rewrite it freely &mdash; this is the most personal page on the site.
      </PlaceholderBanner>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>How this started</h2>
        <p>
          [Josh: where do you live, what is your balcony like &mdash; size, direction, floor, wind? What was the first thing
          you tried to grow, and what went wrong?]
        </p>
        <p>
          Like a lot of renters, I hit the same walls again and again: I can&rsquo;t drill into anything, the balcony has a
          weight limit nobody could quite explain, the wind is brutal up here, and winter shuts everything down. Most
          growing advice assumes a garden. I didn&rsquo;t have one.
        </p>

        <h2>Why Pot and Balcony exists</h2>
        <p>
          I wanted the resource I couldn&rsquo;t find: honest, specific advice for people growing in tiny rented spaces,
          from someone actually doing it. Real photos, real mistakes, real prices &mdash; and no pretending that an
          expensive gadget is essential.
        </p>


        <h2>The long game: a farm</h2>
        <p>
          [Josh: describe your longer-term goal &mdash; the farm, smallholding or land you eventually want, and why. What
          does the balcony teach you that you&rsquo;ll need later? What does &ldquo;success&rdquo; look like in five or ten years?]
        </p>
        <p>
          The balcony is my training ground. Every guide here is a small experiment in growing more with less: less
          space, less time, less money wasted on the wrong kit.
        </p>

        <h2>How this site is made</h2>
        <p>
          I&rsquo;ll be upfront: I use AI tools to help with research, drafting and publishing. What AI can&rsquo;t do is
          stand on my balcony. The photos, the field notes and the verdicts on gear come from me. [Josh: adjust this
          paragraph to describe your process in your own words.]
        </p>

        <h2>Ground rules</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>I only recommend gear I&rsquo;ve actually used &mdash; or I tell you plainly that I haven&rsquo;t.</li>
          <li>Affiliate links are always disclosed, and they never decide what I recommend. <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Details here</a>.</li>
          <li>If I get something wrong, I&rsquo;ll fix it and say so.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Say hello</h2>
        <p>
          Got a question, a correction, or a balcony horror story? <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a> &mdash; I read everything.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero { display: grid; gap: var(--s-7); align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 52rem) { .about-hero { grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 0.6fr; } }
  .about-hero h1 { margin-bottom: var(--s-4); }
  .about-photo { margin: 0; justify-self: center; }
  .about-photo img { width: min(100%, 16rem); aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid var(--forest); background: var(--olive); box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 var(--forest); }
  .about-photo figcaption { font-family: var(--font-hand); font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: var(--s-4); text-align: center; }
  .about-photo em { font-style: normal; opacity: 0.8; }
</style>
